<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The job a social fight is actually fought with (RimWorld: JobDefOf.SocialFight). Its own file, per
    CLAUDE.md. Before it existed, MentalState_SocialFighting swung a verb straight out of its own tick with
    no map, no position and no reach - see that class's doc for what that cost.

    Every flag left at its default deliberately. casualInterruptible was briefly set false here on the
    reasoning that a pawn mid-brawl should not drift off; RimWorld's own value for this JobDef could not be
    read from this environment, and the flag changes nothing that matters either way - a fight interrupted
    by the constant tree is handed straight back by the mental-state tier on the next evaluation, because
    the mental state, not the job, is what decides the fight is still on. Sleep stays the only job in this
    port's content that refuses a casual interrupt, which is a claim one of its tests makes.
  -->

  <JobDef>
    <defName>SocialFight</defName>
    <driverClass>SimWorld.AI.JobDriver_SocialFight</driverClass>
    <reportString>fighting.</reportString>
  </JobDef>

</Defs>
